WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.412
Part three.

00:00:01.412 --> 00:00:04.379
Assertions, verdicts and bug reports.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.405
The last run placed an order.

00:00:07.405 --> 00:00:13.508
But right now the scenario only clicks and types: it never checks that the order was actually confirmed.

00:00:13.533 --> 00:00:15.119
Add an Assert at the end.

00:00:15.119 --> 00:00:19.684
Choose Text contains, then target the confirmation message right on the page.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.055
The text to expect is confirmed.

00:00:31.055 --> 00:00:33.702
Name the step and add it to the scenario.

00:00:38.967 --> 00:00:41.034
Now run the scenario again.

00:00:52.933 --> 00:00:53.718
Passed.

00:00:53.718 --> 00:00:58.604
This time Pocket QA didn't just get through the steps: it proved the order went through.

00:00:58.633 --> 00:01:03.187
Now suppose the developers ship an update, and the order confirmation changes.

00:01:03.833 --> 00:01:05.180
Run it once more.

00:01:22.633 --> 00:01:23.412
Failed.

00:01:23.412 --> 00:01:29.351
The verdict names the failing step: it expected confirmed, but the page says payment pending.

00:01:29.351 --> 00:01:32.326
The toolbar badge turns into a red cross too.

00:01:32.333 --> 00:01:36.524
The dots under the verdict are the scenario's run history, one per run.

00:01:36.524 --> 00:01:43.074
When a test keeps failing after it passed, or fails now and then with the same steps, the card says so.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:49.306
Every run ends with one of four verdicts: Passed, Failed, Test broken when the test itself is at fault,

00:01:49.306 --> 00:01:52.849
like a missing element, and Stopped when you halt it.

00:01:52.867 --> 00:01:54.146
Click Bug report.

00:01:54.146 --> 00:02:01.853
Pocket QA drafts a Markdown report with the URL, the browser, the steps to reproduce, and a screenshot of the failure.

00:02:01.867 --> 00:02:04.988
Typed values and passwords stay hidden by default.

00:02:04.988 --> 00:02:08.543
Copy it, paste it into your issue tracker, and you're done.

00:02:08.567 --> 00:02:12.533
Next, we'll make the scenario smarter with variables and logic.
